{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785697198,"nonce":"wFTbimlVoi3YhLZct6zllHT+P20=","title":"**Live in every deployment, not just warm-only.** Established 2026-08-03 by reading the code.","message":"Log bodies are NOT on the Depot (ADR-0063 is unbuilt; the Depot router has no log route). `LogService::new(store, db)` (`crates/scarab-server/src/main.rs:258`) writes gzipped bodies to the OBJECT STORE and Postgres keeps only offsets (`migrations/0005_log_chunks.sql`). With `SCARAB_S3_BUCKET` unset that store is `StoreConfig::LocalDir` — on the Helm chart, a **control-plane-pod-local dir on the `scratch` emptyDir** (`deployment.yaml:78-108`).\n\n**The bug: the read path SWALLOWS the error.** `.unwrap_or_default()` at `crates/scarab-server/src/lib.rs:1796` and `if let Ok(..)` at `:1972` turn a failed body read into an **empty pane** — the reader is shown a plausible blank instead of being told the bytes are gone. This is exactly the defect ADR-0063 part 5 forbids (\"absence is authoritative; a record-first implementation hands the reader the blank pane this slice exists to prevent\").\n\nTwo consequences beyond the obvious:\n- **Per-replica.** The bodies are on one pod's emptyDir, so with \u003e1 control-plane replica, replica B serves an empty pane for logs replica A holds. Not an eventual-consistency window — permanent.\n- **Silent on every pod roll.** Logs die with the pod and nothing says so.\n\nThis is INDEPENDENT of the object-storage question and of ADR-0063's move to the Depot. Even before either lands, the read path must stop lying.\n\n- [ ] The three branches of ADR-0063 part 5 implemented at the read path: no chunks in the index -\u003e the Step genuinely printed nothing (truthful empty pane); chunks + bytes present -\u003e serve them; chunks + bytes ABSENT -\u003e \"logs are no longer available\"\n- [ ] No `unwrap_or_default()` / `if let Ok` on a log body read anywhere\n- [ ] A test where the index has chunks and the bytes are removed with NO eviction record, asserting the reader is told\n- [ ] Note in the ticket trail whether this is fixed before or after ADR-0063's move to the Depot (the fix is valid either way)","files":null}]}